Summary
The 0/1 Knapsack problem using Dynamic Programming finds the maximum value that can be placed in a knapsack without exceeding its capacity.
Each item can either be selected once or not selected.
A DP table is used to store the best possible value for different capacities and numbers of items.
The algorithm avoids repeated calculations and efficiently finds the optimal solution.

Conclusion
The Dynamic Programming approach provides an efficient way to solve the 0/1 Knapsack problem. 
For n items and knapsack capacity W, its time complexity is O(n × W) and space complexity is O(n × W).
It guarantees the maximum possible value while keeping the total weight within the given capacity.
